    ; ★★ THE DEFAULT ARM IS THE INTERESTING ONE AND ITS TWO TESTS ARE NOT
    ; SYMMETRIC. A function-like node is NOT descended into — the reference's own
    ; comment says a class's methods would require descending into the class and
    ; that is by design — except through a COMPUTED NAME, which is evaluated in
    ; the enclosing scope and so can carry a yield. Everything that is not
    ; function-like descends unless it is part of a TYPE node, where no expression
    ; is evaluated at all.
    function for_each_yield_expression_is_context_sensitive(this, node: ref[AstNode]) returns bool linked


















































    ; isContextSensitive, the twelve-arm dispatch.
    ;
    ; ★★★ ITS FunctionDeclaration ARM IS NOT DEAD CODE EVEN THOUGH NO ARM OF THIS
    ; PORT ASKS ABOUT ONE FROM OUTSIDE: the recursion reaches it through a
    ; property assignment or a parenthesis, and it is the reference's own arm. What
    ; IS unreachable is nothing here — every arm has an input in this corpus.
    ;
    ; ★★ THE BINARY ARM IS TWO OPERATORS AND NOT ALL OF THEM, which is the whole
    ; content of that line: only `||` and `??` propagate a contextual type to both
    ; sides, so `f() || (x => x)` is context sensitive and `a + (x => x)` is not.
    function is_context_sensitive(this, node: ref[AstNode]?) returns bool linked





































































    function some_is_context_sensitive(this, nodes: ref[Array[ref[AstNode]?]]?) returns bool linked














