    ; `any` supplied for each of the class's type parameters (TypeScript 1.0 spec
    ; 8.4). ★★★THE NOTE THAT STOOD AT ITS CALL SITE SAID *the parent walk is
    ; getParentOfSymbol, which this port does not have* — and get_parent_of_symbol
    ; has been in this file for dozens of slices (§3.5eo).
    ;
    ; ★ The reference indexes `AsInterfaceType()` without a guard, because a
    ; prototype's parent is a CLASS and a class's declared type is an interface
    ; type. Here a null answer is reported the way every other absent
    ; precondition is, so the shape that would panic upstream says so instead.
    procedure get_type_of_prototype_property(mutable this, mutable prototype: ref[Symbol]) @page true @returnpage true returns ref[Type]? io reads ordinal_lock linked

























