    ; ── the OBJECT REST type (slice 145) ─────────────────────────────────────
    ;
    ; getRestType — what `{a, ...rest} = o` gives `rest`, and what the object
    ; BINDING pattern's `...rest` gives too. Two call sites, one function, and it
    ; was two rows on the frontier (`get-rest-type` and the assignment chapter's).
    ;
    ; ★★★ THE ANSWER IS A DIFFERENT KIND OF TYPE ON EACH SIDE OF ONE TEST, and the
    ; test is `isGenericObjectType(source) || isGenericIndexType(omitKeyType)`. For a
    ; CONCRETE source it builds an anonymous type out of the spreadable properties
    ; — a real member table, flagged ObjectRestType. For a GENERIC one it cannot
    ; enumerate anything, so it hands back `Omit<Source, Keys>` from the global
    ; type alias and lets instantiation do the work later. A port that built only
    ; the first would answer a member-less object for every generic rest.
    ;
    ; ★★ THE UNSPREADABLE PROPERTIES ARE ADDED TO THE OMIT KEY ONLY ON THE GENERIC
    ; PATH, and the reference says why: *if the type we're spreading from has
    ; properties that cannot be spread into the rest type (e.g. getters, methods),
    ; ensure they are explicitly omitted, as they would in the non-generic case.*
    ; On the concrete path they are omitted by construction — they never enter the
    ; member table — so the same effect needs no key.
    ;
    ; ★ The head filter is the reference's `filterType(source, t.flags&Nullable == 0)`
    ; and filter_type_outside_flags is that predicate: for any constituent a
    ; nullable flag is the WHOLE of its flags, so *has no nullable flag* and *has a
    ; flag outside the nullable mask* pick the same constituents.
    procedure get_rest_type(mutable this, mutable source_in: ref[Type], mutable properties: ref[Array[ref[AstNode]?]]?, mutable symbol: ref[Symbol]?) @page true @direct true returns ref[Type]? io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked
















































































































































    ; getGlobalOmitSymbol — `Omit<T, K>`, the two-parameter alias every generic
    ; object rest is expressed through. ★It answers NULL where the lib does not
    ; declare it, and getRestType turns that into `error_type` rather than into a
    ; report: the reference does the same, because a missing `Omit` has already been
    ; reported by the global-type resolution itself.
    procedure get_global_omit_symbol(mutable this) returns ref[Symbol]? io reads shared_lock linked





    ; isValidSpreadType — the object BINDING pattern's rest guard (slice 145).
    ; ★★ THE UNION ARM RECURSES ON THE FILTERED TYPE'S OWN CONSTITUENTS and not on
    ; the argument's, which matters because the head has already mapped every
    ; constituent to its base constraint and removed the definitely-falsy ones: the
    ; question is about what the spread would actually see.
    procedure is_valid_spread_type(mutable this, mutable t: ref[Type]) returns bool io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked





































