    ; which is exactly what getOptionalExpressionType answers by returning its own
    ; argument when the expression is not a chain link. ★The callee is checked with
    ; check_expression here and NOT with check_non_null_expression — the ordinary
    ; arm's non-null check is what the chain replaces.
    procedure get_return_type_of_single_non_generic_signature_of_call_chain(mutable this, mutable expr: ref[AstNode]) @page true @returnpage true returns ref[Type]? io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked

























    ; getSingleSignature, whole. ★★ `allowMembers` IS THE WHOLE OF THE PROPERTY
    ; TEST: at the one call site above it is TRUE, so a callee type carrying
    ; properties or index signatures still qualifies — the two narrower wrappers
    ; (getSingleCallSignature, getSingleCallOrConstructSignature) pass false and have
    ; no caller here, so they are left out (§3.5be).
    ;
    ; ★ The counting is the point rather than the lookup: EXACTLY ONE signature of
    ; the asked kind and NONE of the other. An overloaded function has two call
    ; signatures and answers nil; a class has one construct signature and no call
    ; signature, which is why `new C()` reaches this at all.
    ; getSingleCallOrConstructSignature — the call signature if there is exactly
    ; one, else the construct one. ★`allowMembers` is FALSE at this call site, so a
    ; type carrying properties beside its one signature answers nothing.
    procedure get_single_call_or_construct_signature(mutable this, mutable t: ref[Type]) returns ref[Signature]? io reads checker_rewrite_relative_import_extensions linked










    procedure get_single_signature(mutable this, mutable t: ref[Type], kind: int, allow_members: bool) returns ref[Signature]? io reads checker_rewrite_relative_import_extensions linked















































    ; isSymbolOrSymbolForCall, WHOLE since slice 146.
