    ; conditionalTypeToTypeNode — the transform the bracket above wraps. It is a
    ; function of its own for exactly that reason: the bracket must pop on every
    ; exit and this body has six.
    ; ★★★ typeToTypeNodeOrCircularityElision (slice 219): a conditional type's
    ; branches are printed through the VISITED set when they are unions — a
    ; union already being printed answers the elision placeholder (`any` under
    ; the harness's noErrorTruncation), an unvisited one is printed through
    ; visitAndTransformType, which ADDS it to the set for the duration (and
    ; counts its symbol's depth where it has one). The recursive conditional of
    ; `arrayFakeFlatNoCrashInferenceDeclarations` has the same union as the
    ; true type of the outer and the inner conditional; the reference prints
    ; the inner as `any`, this port expanded it to the truncation budget. Only
    ; a UNION takes the route — every other branch type prints as before.
    procedure write_type_or_circularity_elision(mutable this, mutable t: ref[Type], mutable out: ref[StringBuilder]) returns bool io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked






















