    procedure write_reused_template_literal_type(mutable this, mutable node: ref[AstNode], mutable out: ref[StringBuilder]) returns bool io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked










































    ; typeParameterToDeclarationWithConstraint: the variance modifiers, the name,
    ; the constraint and the default.
    ;
    ; ★★★ THE CONSTRAINT IS WRITTEN FROM THE ANNOTATION SINCE SLICE 169, and the
    ; paragraph this replaces claimed the opposite for four slices: *the one place
    ; in this slice where the reference has a mechanism this port does not … the
    ; CORPUS is the arbiter and it says the two coincide on every constrained
    ; parameter it holds*. The corpus said no such thing by then — five slices had
    ; each found a shape where they part and each had left a stop — and the mechanism
    ; is written out in write_possibly_reused_type_node above.
    ;
    ; ★ typeParameterToName reduces to the symbol's name: its uniquifying loop is
    ; behind GenerateNamesForShadowedTypeParams, which typeToString does not set.
    procedure write_type_parameter_declaration(mutable this, mutable tp: ref[Type], mutable out: ref[StringBuilder]) returns bool io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked





























































    ; symbolToParameterDeclaration plus parameterToParameterDeclarationName.
    ;
    ; ★★★ THE TWO CheckFlags DISJUNCTS ARE WRITTEN SINCE SLICE 155, AND THE NOTE
    ; THAT CALLED THEM DEAD NAMED A PRODUCER RATHER THAN THE SET OF THEM. It read
    ; *"written by exactly one producer — getExpandedParameters' tuple expansion —
    ; and that producer cannot run"*: true of getExpandedParameters, and never a
    ; complete list. combineUnionOrIntersectionParameters writes both bits, and a
    ; combined parameter has NO DECLARATION at all — `pd` is null there — so
    ; without the disjuncts the printer answered a signature of a union of
    ; function types with neither `...` nor `?`. **A dead-arm claim is a claim
    ; about EVERY producer, and a note can only name the ones that exist.**
    ;
    ; ★ `preserveModifierFlags` is false at every call site this family has (only
    ; `kind == KindConstructor` passes true, and no type name contains one), so the
    ; parameter-property modifiers are never written.
    procedure write_parameter_declaration(mutable this, mutable ps: ref[Symbol], mutable out: ref[StringBuilder]) returns bool io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked






























































    ; EmitResolver.requiresAddingImplicitUndefined at its PARAMETER arm, which is
    ; the only one this printer reaches — the property arm needs the reverse-mapped
    ; symbol links, and nothing here mints one.
    ;
    ; ★ `enclosingDeclaration` is nil at every arrival from typeToString, so
    ; isRequiredInitializedParameter's parameter-property fork answers FALSE rather
