    ; getContainersOfSymbol, reduced. ★★★ THE REDUCTION IS THE NIL ENCLOSING
    ; DECLARATION AGAIN, AND IT REMOVES THREE OF THE FOUR SOURCES:
    ; `getAlternativeContainingModules` is guarded by it, the variable-in-scope
    ; search walks the same empty scope chain, and the `container is in scope`
    ; preference fork tests it directly. What is left of getWithAlternativeContainers
    ; is `additionalContainers ++ [container] ++ objectLiteralContainer`, and the
    ; first and last are the `export =` file symbol and an object literal's
    ; variable — neither of which a namespace or class container has. So the answer
    ; is the PARENT, and the candidate branch below it (a symbol with no parent but
    ; a module-level declaration) reports instead of guessing.
    ; getContainersOfSymbol + getWithAlternativeContainers: the containers a chain
    ; may climb through, best first. A parent symbol is the container when the
    ; symbol has one (and is not a type parameter); otherwise the candidates come
    ; from the declarations' module parents.
