    ; The same literal WITHOUT the emit flag, which is the enum member's indexed
    ; access (slice 116): `newStringLiteral` is built there with no EmitFlags at
    ; all, so getLiteralText's NeverAsciiEscape is off and a non-ASCII name is
    ; written as `\uXXXX`.
    procedure write_ascii_escaped_literal_name(mutable out: ref[StringBuilder], text: Slice[char]) linked


    ; getLiteralText's StringLiteral arm, with the delimiter the node's
    ; TokenFlagsSingleQuote selects. ★The two callers are not symmetric: a string
    ; literal TYPE's name is built with no token flags at all and is therefore always
    ; double-quoted, while a property NAME carries the flag from its declarations.
    procedure write_quoted_literal_name(mutable out: ref[StringBuilder], text: Slice[char], quote_char: int, never_ascii_escape: bool) linked






    ; `jsnum.ParsePseudoBigInt(text)` followed by NewPseudoBigInt's
    ; `strings.TrimLeft(value, "0")` — the two steps between a bigint literal's
    ; TEXT and the digits a PseudoBigInt holds, with the all-zero case answering
    ; the EMPTY string the reference represents zero as. Answers the length and
    ; writes the START OFFSET into `out` through `out_start`, or -1 when
    ; ParsePseudoBigInt refuses the text.
    procedure pseudo_big_int_digits(text: Slice[char], mutable out: Slice[char], mutable out_start: ref[int]) returns int linked
















    ; ── printer/utilities.go's escapeStringWorker ───────────────────────────
    ;
    ; ★★★ THE "ALWAYS A DOUBLE QUOTE" HALF OF THIS NARROWING WAS FALSE AND ONLY STAGE
    ; 2 FOUND IT. The note read *"the quote character is always the double quote
    ; (nodeBuilder passes isSingleQuote false and never sets
    ; FlagsUseSingleQuotesForStringLiteralType)"* — and the FLAG does not come from a
    ; parameter at all: createPropertyNameNodeForIdentifierOrLiteral stamps
    ; `TokenFlagsSingleQuote` onto the SYNTHESIZED literal when every declaration of
    ; the symbol is single-quoted (isSingleQuotedStringNamed), and getLiteralText
    ; reads that flag off the node. So `{ 'stage-0': T }` prints with single quotes,
    ; and this port printed double. **A narrowing that names the wrong INPUT is
    ; indistinguishable from a correct one until the other input appears.**
    ;
    ; ★★ THE QUOTE CHARACTER IS THE ESCAPE TRIGGER AND NOT THE ESCAPE TABLE. The
    ; reference's `case rune(quoteChar)` is what decides, while escapedCharsMap
    ; carries BOTH `\"` and `\'` unconditionally — so inside a single-quoted name a
    ; double quote is written BARE and an apostrophe is escaped, which is the
    ; opposite of the double-quoted case and is why the parameter had to reach the
    ; trigger rather than only the delimiters.
    ;
    ; What is still narrowed, and honestly: the flags are always
    ; NeverAsciiEscape and never JsxAttributeEscape (the emit flag the builder adds
    ; is exactly EFNoAsciiEscaping). So the three arms that read `quoteChar ==
    ; backtick`, the whole JSX branch and the `ch > 0x7f` half of the default test
    ; are all decided here rather than carried.
    ;
    ; ★★ WHAT SURVIVES THE NARROWING IS THE PART THAT ACTUALLY BITES: the canonical
    ; escapes, the sub-0x20 controls, the three line-ish code points U+2028,
    ; U+2029 and U+0085, and the SURROGATE cases — a lone surrogate and a
    ; supplementary code point both become `\uXXXX` sequences, uppercase hex, and a
    ; supplementary one becomes TWO of them.
    ;
    ; ★★★ THE DECODER IS `DecodeJSStringRune` AND NOT PLAIN UTF-8, which is the one
    ; place this could have been silently wrong: the scanner writes a lone
    ; surrogate out as its three-byte sentinel (see value_put_codepoint), and Go's
    ; own utf8 decoder REFUSES that encoding and answers RuneError — so a port
    ; reaching for the ordinary decoder would print U+FFFD where the reference
    ; prints `\uD800`.
    procedure escape_string_worker(mutable out: ref[StringBuilder], s: Slice[char], quote_char: int, never_ascii_escape: bool) linked

















































































































































    ; One of a template literal type's texts, through escapeStringWorker with the
    ; BACKTICK delimiter and NeverAsciiEscape — the flag the checker's own printer
    ; carries in its options (createPrinterWithRemoveCommentsNeverAsciiEscape).
