    function is_type_reference_identifier(node: ref[AstNode]) returns bool linked


















    ; getTypeOfExpression, without the FLOW TYPE CACHE — and the omission changes no
    ; answer, which is why it is an omission rather than a report: the cache is
    ; keyed on the node and filled with the very type the call just computed, so a
    ; hit and a miss return the same type. What it costs is the re-analysis, and
    ; `flowInvocationCount` exists upstream only to decide whether caching is worth
    ; it. ★ The reference's CheckModeTypeOnly is passed through, and this port's
    ; check_expression_ex already reads it (its diagnostics gate).
    ; getTypeOfExpression.
    ;
    ; ★★★ ITS CACHE IS OBSERVABLE AND SLICE 120 IS WHERE THAT WAS MEASURED. The
    ; body used to be the quick path plus `check_expression_ex`, i.e. a fresh
    ; check on every ask — and this function is asked by the CONTEXTUAL-TYPE
    ; machinery, which walks up to an assignment and checks its LEFT. Every such
    ; ask therefore REPORTS again, so the number of asks is part of the answer:
    ; `(h, h).b = { c: 2 }` reports TS2695 twice upstream and three times without
    ; the cache. ★The reference's condition is the interesting half — it caches
    ; only when the check it just ran actually did control-flow analysis, tested
    ; by whether `flowInvocationCount` MOVED — so a cheap expression is re-checked
    ; (and re-reports) and an expensive one is not.
    ;
    ; ★ A null is NOT cached, and that line is this port's own: a null here means
    ; the check STOPPED, and a cached stop would answer a later ask without
    ; reporting one.
    procedure get_type_of_expression(mutable this, mutable node: ref[AstNode]) @page true @returnpage true returns ref[Type]? io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked




















    ; getRegularTypeOfExpression. The hop to the parent is what makes `a.b` answer
    ; for the whole access rather than for the name: a right-hand component has no
    ; type of its own.
    procedure get_regular_type_of_expression(mutable this, mutable expr: ref[AstNode]) @page true @returnpage true returns ref[Type]? io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked














