    function check_meta_property_keyword(this, node: ref[AstNode]) returns ref[Type]? linked


    ; ── getSymbolAtLocation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ;
    ; A prefix chain of five context tests followed by a KIND dispatch, and its
    ; shape is kept because the prefix is what the ported arms need: a DECLARATION
    ; NAME answers `getSymbolOfDeclaration(parent)` before the dispatch is reached,
    ; which is the arm getTypeOfNode's name arms live on.
    ;
    ; ★★★ WHAT REPORTS AND WHY EACH ONE HAS TO. Nine of the dispatch's arms need
    ; machinery this slice does not have — resolveExternalModuleName, the JSX
    ; intrinsic tag symbol, getGlobalImportMetaExpressionType, the `instanceof`
    ; right-hand type, getTypeFromThisTypeNode, getSignatureFromDeclaration's this
    ; parameter — and every one of them is a position where the reference answers a
    ; SYMBOL. Falling through to null would make the caller answer errorType, i.e.
    ; `any`, which is 43 % of the corpus's type answers and therefore the single
    ; easiest way to look right while being wrong (getTypeOfNode's own header). So
    ; each reports with the node's kind as the detail.
    ;
    ; ★ `ignore_errors` is threaded because resolveExternalModuleName takes it; no
    ; ported arm reads it yet, and it stays in the signature rather than being
    ; dropped and re-added.
    procedure get_symbol_at_location(mutable this, mutable node: ref[AstNode], ignore_errors: bool) @page true @returnpage true returns ref[Symbol]? io reads ordinal_lock linked































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































