    ;     import a = |b|;      // Namespace
    ;     import a = |b.c|;    // Value, type, namespace
    ;     import a = |b.c|.d;  // Namespace
    ;
    ; ★★ THE FIRST STEP CLIMBS OUT OF THE NAME rather than resolving it: the `c` of
    ; `b.c.d` is the RIGHT side of a qualified name, so what has to be resolved is
    ; the qualified name `b.c` and not the identifier. Resolving the identifier
    ; would ask for a NAMESPACE called `c` in the outer scope.
    ;
    ; ★ The reference's `debug.Assert` on the third case is not written as a row:
    ; the meaning set is the only thing the two branches differ in, and both are
    ; resolve_entity_name with dontResolveAlias TRUE — the whole point of the
    ; function, since the alias must not be followed to what it names.
