    ; ★★ THE TWO SHAPES ARE `x.push(v)` / `x.unshift(v)` AND `x[n] = v`, and they are
    ; told apart on the flow node's KIND rather than on anything about the reference:
    ; a Call gets every ARGUMENT added, an assignment gets its RIGHT side added and
    ; only when the INDEX is number-like. ★The index is asked through
    ; get_context_free_type_of_expression and the reference says why: *we must get
    ; the context free expression type so as to not recur in an uncached fashion on
    ; the LHS (which causes exponential blowup in compile time).*
    procedure get_type_at_flow_array_mutation(mutable this, mutable f: ref[FlowState], mutable flow: ref[FlowNode], mutable out_incomplete: ref[bool]) returns ref[Type]? io reads ordinal_lock linked






































































































