    ; ── the EVOLVING ARRAY, slice 141 ───────────────────────────────────────
    ;
    ; The reference's own comment is the boundary and it is the reason this family
    ; is invisible to every yardstick in this directory until it is COMPLETE: *an
    ; evolving array type tracks the element types that have so far been seen in an
    ; `x.push(value)` or `x[n] = value` operation along the control flow graph.
    ; Evolving array types are ultimately converted into manifest array types
    ; (using getFinalArrayType) and never escape the getFlowTypeOfReference
    ; function.* So the type the dump can see is always the FINAL array type, and a
    ; half-ported family answers a manifest array with the wrong element type
    ; rather than nothing at all.
    ;
    ; ★★★ WHAT THE NOTE THAT STOOD HERE CLAIMED, AND WHY IT EXPIRED. It read
    ; *"finalizeEvolvingArrayType IS ITS OWN GUARD ON THIS CORPUS … new_object_type
    ; refuses ObjectFlagsEvolvingArray, so no type reaching here can carry the
    ; bit"* — a claim about the MINT, correct when it was written and discharged by
    ; this slice at the line that refused the bit. §3.5be's rule the other way
    ; round: a flag with no writer is not a fact about the language, it is a
    ; measurement with an expiry date.
    ;
    ; ★ getUnionOrEvolvingArrayType is the ONE exit every antecedent join takes, so
    ; it is written here beside the family rather than in the branch label that
    ; used to stop on it.

    ; getEvolvingArrayType. c.cachedTypes[CachedTypeKindEvolvingArrayType],
    ; array_literal_type_link_of's idiom at the third kind this port reads.
    ;
    ; ★★ THE MEMO IS LOAD-BEARING AND NOT AN OPTIMISATION, for the reason the
    ; array-literal memo is: `isEvolvingArrayTypeList` and the two subset tests
    ; compare TYPE IDENTITY, so two asks for the evolving array over one element
    ; type must answer the same object or a join of two paths that agree reads as a
    ; join of two paths that differ.
    procedure get_evolving_array_type(mutable this, mutable element_type: ref[Type]) @page true @returnpage true returns ref[Type]? linked













