    ; ── slice 108: the call's RESOLUTION ────────────────────────────────────
    ;
    ; `is-untyped-function-call 214` — 52 events over 33 units at stage 1, 1 322
    ; units and 4 881 events at stage 2 — the largest row slice 107 could name that
    ; is neither the lib nor a name resolution. What stood there was one
    ; `record_unported` after getSignaturesOfType, and the function it is named
    ; after is four disjuncts.
    ;
    ; ★★★ THE ROW IS NOT THE CHAPTER, AND A PROBE SAID SO BEFORE A LINE WAS
    ; WRITTEN. Replacing the stop's tag argument by a bitfield over the four
    ; disjuncts' own inputs — and then by `ncall*1000 + single_non_generic*100 +
    ; nargs*10 + ntypeargs` — reports 50 of the 52 arrivals as **one call signature
    ; that is not generic**, i.e. every one of them passes every disjunct of
    ; `isUntypedFunctionCall` and falls through to `resolveCall`. Only TWO are
    ; untyped calls, both `any` on both sides. **So the wall behind a row named
    ; after a predicate was the OVERLOAD RESOLUTION, and the predicate answers
    ; FALSE for 96 % of its own population.** ★★A stop's tag names the first thing
    ; the porter could not do, never the shape of what arrives — and the only
    ; instrument that separates the two is a probe on the stop's own argument.
    ;
    ; ★★★ WHICH IS WHY THIS SLICE IS BOUNDED BY `chooseOverload`'s FIRST ARM AND
    ; NOT BY THE ROW. `s.isSingleNonGenericCandidate` is exactly the 47 of 52
    ; arrivals that also carry no type arguments, and its arm is three lines:
    ; hasCorrectArity, then isSignatureApplicable, then the candidate. The
    ; multi-candidate loop underneath it needs inferTypeArguments, the inference
    ; context and getSignatureInstantiation, and it is a row.
    ;
    ; ★★★ AND THE HEAD MESSAGE IS NOT THREADED THROUGH THE RELATION, WHICH IS THE
    ; MEASUREMENT THAT SAVED THE SLICE'S WIDEST EDIT. `isSignatureApplicable` hands
    ; `Argument_of_type_0_is_not_assignable_to_parameter_of_type_1` (TS2345) to
    ; checkTypeRelatedToAndOptionallyElaborate, and TS2345 is a CODE — so a `C` line
    ; depends on it and the parameter looked mandatory. It is not: `chooseOverload`
    ; passes `reportErrors` FALSE at every call, `errorNode` is therefore nil, and
    ; the relation returns before any message is selected. The reporting pass that
    ; passes TRUE is `reportCallResolutionErrors`, and that is this slice's wall —
    ; so a `head_message` parameter added here would be **a parameter with a writer
    ; and no reader**, slice 67's finding two in the other direction.
    ;
    ; ★★ WHAT THE SLICE ANSWERS is a SIGNATURE, and the diagnostics are a
    ; by-product: check_call_expression already asks get_return_type_of_signature,
    ; so a call whose one candidate has the right arity and assignable arguments now
    ; has a TYPE. The four codes it can emit — TS2347, TS2348, TS2349, TS2351 — all
    ; sit on the paths where resolution does NOT happen.

    ; The list length of a signature array, which is `len(...)` at seven sites here.
    ; ★It is a static and not a method for the reason the file's other `*_count`
    ; statics are: it asks nothing of the checker.
    function sig_count(a: ref[Array[ref[Signature]?]]?) returns int linked






    ; Its two siblings, slice 119, for the same `len(...)` at the same shape.
