    ; isUntypedFunctionCall, whole — "TS 1.0 spec: 4.12. If FuncExpr is of type Any,
    ; or of an object type that has no call or construct signatures but is a subtype
    ; of the Function interface, the call is an untyped function call."
    ;
    ; ★★★ ITS THIRD DISJUNCT ENDS IN `globalFunctionType` AND IS THEREFORE §3.11,
    ; AND THE CONTAINMENT IS WHAT MAKES THAT SURVIVABLE: four conjuncts stand in
    ; front of the lib term, and the corpus fails the FIRST of them — a call whose
    ; callee has a call signature — at every one of the 50 arrivals a probe counted.
    ; So the row is written at the lib term rather than at the function's door, and
    ; it reads ZERO at stage 1.
    ;
    ; ★★ THE UNION EXCLUSION IS THE REFERENCE'S OWN COMMENT and not an optimisation:
    ; "We exclude union types because we may have a union of function types that
    ; happen to have no common signatures." It is asked before getReducedType, which
    ; is what keeps this function off get_reduced_type's union row.
    procedure is_untyped_function_call(mutable this, mutable func_type: ref[Type], mutable apparent_func_type: ref[Type], num_call_signatures: int, num_construct_signatures: int) returns bool io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked




































