    procedure has_correct_arity_tail(mutable this, node: ref[AstNode], args: ref[Array[ref[AstNode]?]]?, mutable signature: ref[Signature], arg_count: int, effective_parameter_count: int, effective_minimum_arguments: int, call_is_incomplete: bool) returns bool io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked












































    ; isSignatureApplicable, minus the `this`-argument comparison and the spread
    ; tail.
    ;
    ; ★★★ IT IS CALLED WITH `reportErrors` FALSE AND THAT DECIDES THE WHOLE SHAPE OF
    ; THE CHAPTER: with no error node the relation answers and says nothing, so this
    ; function is a PREDICATE here and the head message it would carry has no reader
    ; (see the chapter header). The parameter is kept because
    ; reportCallResolutionErrors passes TRUE, and that is the row above.
    ;
    ; ★★ THE `this`-ARGUMENT COMPARISON IS A ROW BEHIND A CONDITION, not in front of
    ; one: getThisTypeOfSignature answers non-nil only for a signature with an
    ; explicit `this` parameter, so the row's population is exactly those signatures
    ; and the corpus's ordinary call never reaches it. What it needs is
    ; getThisArgumentOfCall over SkipOuterExpressions, getThisArgumentType with its
    ; two optional-chain arms, and a checkTypeRelatedToEx that REPORTS — the head
    ; message again.
    ;
    ; ★ CheckModeSkipContextSensitive is never set at this call site (argCheckMode is
    ; Normal for a single non-generic candidate), so getRegularTypeOfObjectLiteral is
    ; not asked and `checkArgType` is the argument's own type.
