    ; `typeArguments.End()`, where a NodeList's Pos is just after the `<` and its
    ; End just after the last element. The first element's Pos is the same position
    ; (a node's Pos runs back to the previous token's end) and the last element's
    ; End is the list's End, so the pair is recoverable from the elements — except
    ; behind a TRAILING COMMA, where upstream's End sits after the comma and this
    ; one before it.
