    ; compiler — getRegularTypeOfObjectLiteral passing ITSELF — so the parameter is
    ; a recursion and not a hook. Scaly can spell a delegate, but a delegate whose
    ; only value is the enclosing function would be an indirect call for a
    ; self-reference, and §3.5dj is the standing argument against a parameter with
    ; one caller.
    ;
    ; ★★ `updated != original` IS A POINTER TEST and it is what keeps the table
    ; SHARED in the common case: a property whose type is not itself a fresh object
    ; literal keeps its own symbol, so no new symbol is minted and the regular twin
    ; and the fresh one name the same members.
