    ; ── internal/evaluator/evaluator.go ─────────────────────────────────────
    ;
    ; The closure's body, whole. ★★ THE THREE LOCALS ARE THE POINT of the
    ; reference's shape and are transcribed as locals here: an arm that cannot
    ; produce a VALUE still contributes `resolvedOtherFiles` and
    ; `hasExternalReferences` to the answer, so the fall-through at the foot is
    ; not `nil` — it is nil WITH the flags the arm collected. Reading the tail as
    ; a plain failure is how a cross-file enum reference loses its mark.
    procedure evaluate(mutable this, mutable expr_in: ref[AstNode]?, location: ref[AstNode]?) @page true @direct true returns EvalResult io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked

































































































































































    ; `leftStr + rightStr`, with either side stringified first through jsnum's own
