    ; evaluateEntity — the callback NewEvaluator is built over, and the only part
    ; of the evaluator that knows what a symbol is.
    ;
    ; ★★ THE `Infinity` / `NaN` ARM IS A GLOBALS QUESTION AND THE REFERENCE SAYS
    ; WHY IN ITS OWN COMMENT: the decision to read the identifier as numeric rests
    ; on the single-file resolution NOT having found a different meaning for the
    ; name. So it is `symbol == getGlobalSymbol(text)` — an identity test against
    ; the lib's own symbol — and it needs the globals table slice 113 built.
    ;
    ; ★ The reference PANICS on any other kind ("Unhandled case in evaluateEntity").
    ; Its two callers are `evaluate`'s Identifier arm and its access arms, so the
    ; unreachable third case is answered with `none` here rather than trapped, for
    ; the reason jsnum_parse_pseudo_big_int's own refusal gives: a trap would be a
    ; claim about the input, where this is a claim about the callers.
    procedure evaluate_entity(mutable this, mutable expr: ref[AstNode], location: ref[AstNode]?) @page true @direct true returns EvalResult io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked





































    ; The Identifier / PropertyAccessExpression half of evaluateEntity — one Go
    ; `case` with two kinds, split out because the element-access half shares none
    ; of it.
    procedure evaluate_entity_name(mutable this, mutable expr: ref[AstNode], location: ref[AstNode]?) @page true @direct true returns EvalResult io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked













































































    ; evaluateEnumMember, whole. ★ Both reports name a message with an argument
    ; the yardstick does not compare — tscaly_types dumps `C pos end code` — so
    ; symbolToString is not needed here, which is what makes the arm portable at
    ; all in this slice.
    procedure evaluate_enum_member(mutable this, expr: ref[AstNode], mutable symbol: ref[Symbol], location: ref[AstNode]) @page true @direct true returns EvalResult io reads shared_lock linked
























