    ; resolveDecorator.
    ;
    ; ★★★ THE ZERO-SIGNATURE REPORT IS A CHAIN UPSTREAM AND ONE LINE HERE, and the
    ; two agree on what the yardstick sees. `NewDiagnosticChain(details, head)`
    ; takes the CHAIN's location and the HEAD's code, the details' location is
    ; `errorTarget` — the decorator's expression, whose parent is the Decorator and
    ; therefore not a CallExpression, so neither invocationErrorDetails' property-
    ; access rewrite nor its get-accessor head can fire — and the dump is
    ; `C pos end code`. So the honest transcription is: report the decorator head's
    ; code at the expression. invocationErrorRecovery is not written, for
    ; invocation_error's own recorded reason.
    procedure resolve_decorator(mutable this, mutable node: ref[AstNode], check_mode: int) @page true @returnpage true returns ref[Signature]? io reads ordinal_lock linked











































































    ; checkDecorator.
    ;
    ; ★ The `returnType.flags & Any` early exit is what keeps the ordinary
    ; `declare function d(...args: any[]): any` decorator silent: an `any` return
    ; is assignable to anything, so the comparison below would say nothing anyway.
    procedure check_decorator(mutable this, mutable node: ref[AstNode]) io reads ordinal_lock linked































































    ; checkGrammarPrivateIdentifierExpression, whole — upstream's grammarchecks.go.
    ;
    ; ★★★ THE THREE REPORTS ARE A CHAIN AND THE FOR-IN GUARD SUPPRESSES THE LAST
    ; TWO, NOT THE FIRST. `for (#x in obj)` is a parse-level shape the reference
    ; lets through here on purpose — the left operand of a for-in is not an
    ; expression node, so without the guard EVERY such head would report TS1451 —
    ; while a private name outside any class body is illegal wherever it stands.
    ;
    ; ★★ TS2304 IS REPORTED ONLY WHERE THE `in` OPERATION IS NOT, and that is not
    ; the same test as is_expression_node's: that arm has already established the
    ; node IS the left operand of an `in`, so `isInOperation` can only be true on
    ; a node that passed the line above. It is transcribed as the reference has it
    ; rather than folded away, because the two conditions are separated by a
    ; report and folding them would move the TS1451.
    procedure check_grammar_private_identifier_expression(mutable this, mutable priv_id: ref[AstNode]) returns bool reads ordinal_lock linked







































    ; checkGrammarDecorator, whole.
    ;
    ; ★★★ THE LOOP IS A DESCENT AND `canHaveCallExpression` IS ITS ONE PIECE OF
    ; STATE: `@a.b.c()` is legal, `@a().b` is not, because a call may appear only
    ; at the OUTERMOST position of a decorator's expression. The flag is cleared by
    ; the first call or member hop and read by the next call, which is the whole
    ; grammar.
    ;
    ; ★★ THE RELATED INFO IS DROPPED AND THE DIAGNOSTIC IS NOT — the same reading
    ; check_grammar_for_use_strict_simple_parameter_list' header makes.
    ; `err.AddRelatedInfo(createDiagnosticForNode(errorNode, Invalid_syntax_in_decorator))`
    ; puts TS1498 ON the TS1497 rather than in the list, so no dump reaches it. The
    ; error node is therefore computed and used only as a FLAG here, and the report
    ; lands on the decorator's expression exactly as upstream's does.
    procedure check_grammar_decorator(mutable this, decorator: ref[AstNode]) returns bool reads shared_lock linked



















































































    ; markDecoratorAliasReferenced — markLinkedReferences' DECORATOR arm.
    ;
    ; ★★ A PROVABLE NO-OP UNDER THIS HARNESS AND WRITTEN AS ITS OWN FIRST LINE:
    ; `EmitDecoratorMetadata.IsFalseOrUnknown()` is TRUE for an unset option, so
    ; the serialized-metadata walk below it — a checkExternalEmitHelpers call, the
    ; constructor/accessor/method/property/parameter type nodes and
    ; markEntityNameOrEntityExpressionAsReference — is unreachable. It is a
    ; procedure rather than a line in mark_linked_references so that the day an
    ; options record arrives, this is the one body that fills.
    ; markDecoratorAliasReferenced (slice 248): under emitDecoratorMetadata the
    ; type names a decorated member's signature carries are VALUE references —
    ; the alias they resolve through must survive import elision.
    ; ★checkExternalEmitHelpers(Metadata) is a diagnostic about tslib and is not
