    ; comment is the reason: *obtaining the contextual type may recursively get
    ; back to here during overload resolution of the call*, so the flag can have
    ; been set by the recursion between the two reads. The second test is the one
    ; that matters and the first is the cheap one; collapsing them would be a
    ; behaviour change the day a call site re-enters.
