    ; which need the Checker. Upstream every mapper implementation that needs one
    ; carries a `c *Checker` field; here the receiver is the same thing spelled once
    ; instead of per arm. ★The Merged arm makes it recursive, which a static
    ; function could have done and a method does the same way.
    procedure type_mapper_map(mutable this, mutable m: ref[TypeMapper], mutable t: ref[Type]?) @page true @returnpage true returns ref[Type]? io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked


































































































































































































    ; TypeMapper.MapsThisOnly.
    function type_mapper_maps_this_only(m: ref[TypeMapper]) returns bool linked






































    ; isNonGenericTopLevelType, WRITTEN OUT SINCE SLICE 139.
    ;
    ; ★★★ THE NOTE THAT STOOD HERE NAMED ITS OWN EXPIRY CONDITION — *the day the
    ; alias slot arrives, one body changes and no caller does* — AND THE SLOT
    ; ARRIVED IN SLICE 111, WHICH MADE THE CONSTANT `false` A STACK OVERFLOW. It is
    ; the RECURSION GUARD of could_contain_type_variables, on both its arms: a
    ; top-level non-generic type ALIAS is where the walk must stop, and a RECURSIVE
    ; alias is exactly where it otherwise cannot. `type Expression =
    ; BooleanLogicExpression | 'true' | 'false'` with `type BooleanLogicExpression =
    ; ['and', ...Expression[]] | ['not', Expression]` recursed until the stack ran
    ; out — SIGSEGV, all six artifacts of one unit at once, which reads as a harness
    ; failure and not as a checker one. It only became reachable when this slice
    ; removed the walls in front of it (§3.5fq: a wall hides wrong answers).
    ;
    ; ★ The ancestor walk is the reference's `FindAncestorOrQuit`: a SourceFile is
    ; the match, a ModuleDeclaration keeps walking, and ANY other parent quits — so
    ; an alias inside a namespace body is not top-level, because its parent is the
    ; ModuleBlock and that is the quit case.
    function is_non_generic_top_level_type(t: ref[Type]) returns bool linked



























    ; couldContainTypeVariablesWorker, whole, memo included.
    ;
    ; ★★★ IT IS THE GATE IN FRONT OF EVERY instantiateType AND ITS ANSWER IS `false`
    ; FOR ALMOST EVERYTHING THIS CHAPTER TOUCHES — a `number` annotation, a
    ; non-generic class's own declared type (whose type arguments are the EMPTY
    ; list), an index signature's value type. That is what keeps instantiate_type's
    ; unported arms unreached rather than merely unwritten, and g-rows of the
    ; battery measure it.
    ;
    ; ★ It REPORTS, because getTypeArguments does — so its callers check the mark,
    ; the idiom is_thisless_interface' callers already use. The memo is written
    ; only on a complete answer: a half-computed `false` cached under
    ; CouldContainTypeVariablesComputed would outlive the stop that produced it.
    procedure could_contain_type_variables(mutable this, mutable t: ref[Type]) returns bool io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked




































































































































    ; ── the active-mapper stack (slice 163) ─────────────────────────────────
    ;
    ; findActiveMapper / pushActiveMapper / popActiveMapper /
    ; clearActiveMapperCaches. ONE stack of ActiveMapper records where upstream has
    ; two parallel slices — the record's header carries the mapping decision and
    ; what the memo is for.

    ; core.FindLastIndex over c.activeMappers. ★LAST and not first: the same mapper
    ; can be pushed at two depths, and the entry an outer frame is filling is the
    ; one nearest the top.
    function find_active_mapper(this, m: ref[TypeMapper]) returns int linked






















    ; pushActiveMapper. A row past the count is one pop_active_mapper left
    ; behind: its `entries` list is already empty (the pop clears it, as upstream's
    ; does) and only the mapper has to be re-pointed.
    procedure push_active_mapper(mutable this, m: ref[TypeMapper]) linked






















    ; popActiveMapper — the level leaves the stack and its memo is CLEARED, which
    ; is upstream's own `clear(...)` and not tidiness: the row is reused by the next
    ; push, and an entry taken under the previous occupant of this level is keyed on
    ; a mapper nobody will compare against again.
    procedure pop_active_mapper(mutable this) linked

















    ; clearActiveMapperCaches — every LIVE level's memo is dropped, the stack
    ; itself stays. ★★★ IT IS A CORRECTNESS CALL AND NOT A HOUSEKEEPING ONE:
    ; getInferredType calls it the moment an inference is settled, because an
    ; InferenceTypeMapper asked before and after that moment answers differently,
    ; and an entry taken under such a mapper is then a wrong answer with nothing to
    ; say so.
