    ; ── instantiateMappedType and its three constituent arms ────────────────
    ;
    ; ★★★ THE REFERENCE'S OWN COMMENT IS THE SPECIFICATION and it is worth
    ; keeping: for a homomorphic `{ [P in keyof T]: X }` the mapping DEPENDS on
    ; what T becomes — a primitive maps to itself, a union distributes, an array
    ; maps to an array of transformed elements, a tuple to a tuple, an
    ; intersection of those to an intersection, and anything else to an object
    ; type with each property transformed.
    procedure instantiate_mapped_type(mutable this, mutable t: ref[Type], mutable m: ref[TypeMapper]?, alias: ref[TypeAlias]?) @page true @direct true returns ref[Type]? io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked





















































