    ; matching property NAME with a disagreeing LITERAL type is as good a
    ; refutation as a missing property. Dropping the arm made the first call
    ; answer the second's question, so `{ kind: "a" }` against `{ kind: "b" }`
    ; was *not definitely unrelated* and the inference went on to relate them.
