    ; ★★★ THE AWAIT HALF IS DROPPED AND THE ANSWER IS NOT, which is the rule
    ; check_this_expression's TS7041 note states from its own side: `isAwaitValid`
    ; decides only whether `Did_you_forget_to_use_await` is ATTACHED as related
    ; information, and AddRelatedInfo keeps a second span ON the diagnostic rather
    ; than in the list — tscaly_types dumps `C pos end code`, so no yardstick can
    ; see one in either direction. ★★What makes it a decision rather than a saving
    ; is the WALK: `getAwaitedTypeOfPromise` would run getAwaitedType over a
    ; promise's type argument, which this port cannot do, and a stop there would
    ; take the unit out of the comparison for a span nothing compares. The
