    ; ★★★ ITS CONDITION IS THE MESSAGE: some call (or construct) signature of the
    ; source has a return type that IS related to the target, and neither `any`
    ; nor `never` — the two that relate to everything and would make the note fire
    ; for every failing call. Only then is the relation re-asked WITH the error
    ; node, so the ordinary TS2322 is emitted at the expression and the note is
    ; attached to it.
