    ; elaborateError, whole.
    ;
    ; ★★★ ITS FOUR ELABORATING ARMS HAVE NO INPUT AND THE PROOF IS ONE SENTENCE:
    ; an object literal, an array literal, an arrow function and a JSX attributes
    ; list all have an OBJECT type, `source` IS that expression's type, and this
    ; function is reached only after is_type_related_to answered without stopping —
    ; which for an Object source it cannot, because the structured branch stops.
    ; They are written as reports rather than left out, so the slice that opens the
    ; recursion meets them at the reference's own fork.
    ;
    ; ★★ `elaborateDidYouMeanToCallOrConstruct` IS LEFT OUT WITH A VERIFIED
    ; CONTAINMENT, and it is the one claim in this chapter that rests on lib.d.ts
    ; rather than on this port. It asks whether the SOURCE has a call or construct
    ; signature whose return type is related to the target; `getSignaturesOfType`
    ; answers through the APPARENT type, which for every non-structured source is a
    ; global wrapper interface — and none of String, Number, Boolean, BigInt,
    ; Symbol, Object or Function-less `void`/`null`/`undefined` declares a call or
    ; a construct signature at the INSTANCE side (checked in the pinned submodule's
    ; own lib.es5.d.ts). ★The second half of this note — *the port could not ask the
    ; question if it wanted to: get_apparent_type reports `global-apparent-type` for
    ; exactly those flags* — expired in slice 154, which gave those five arms the
    ; reference's own answer; the containment above never rested on it.
    ;
    ; ★ `isOrHasGenericConditional(target)` needs Conditional or an Intersection
    ; holding one, both structured; and `compilerOptions.NoCheck` is unset, which
    ; is the plain-equality reading of an unset option (§3.5cw).
