    ; the whole reason the simplification is sound: a restrictive instantiation
    ; replaces every type parameter's constraint with `unknown`, so an assignable
    ; answer holds for EVERY instantiation of the conditional rather than for the
    ; one in hand. Asking `isTypeAssignableTo(checkType, extendsType)` directly
    ; would simplify a conditional whose branch depends on a type argument nobody
    ; has supplied yet.
