    ; POSITION BY POSITION where the general path slices the source, and for
    ; `[A, B]` against `[T, U]` those are different answers only when the general
    ; path's slicing is wrong. It is written first for the same reason upstream
    ; writes it first — the arms below it all assume the shapes differ.
    procedure infer_from_tuple_target(mutable this, mutable n: ref[InferenceState], mutable source: ref[Type], mutable target: ref[Type]) io reads checker_strict_null_checks linked












































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































